# Persistent-state lane

- STATE.md owns verified current runtime truth, not a roadmap.
- MEMORY.md records durable source-backed findings; append corrections rather
  than erasing history.
- CONTEXT.md is a compact retrieval index. Keep exact paths, symbols, evidence,
  and authority links.
- NOTEPAD.md is active scratch, never a substitute for evidence or canon.
- BRAINSTORM.md is non-canonical exploration. Do not promote speculation.
- ANTITHESIS.md owns rejected directions and recurring anti-drift constraints.
- SCOPE.md names the active Code Forge unit, or records that the last unit
  closed. Do not leave an obsolete unit looking current.
- SOTA_RUN.md is the latest production-code run ledger. A continuity-doc
  update is not a new SOTA run.
- Do not hand-edit filetree.md; regenerate it with FileTree Pro after
  structural changes.
- Do not claim a behavioral change unless the owning source/configuration and a
  matching verification surface changed.
- Next justified action lives in STATE.md: qemu-img / qemu-system-x86_64 plus
  an Android image, or a real _run_inference owner. Do not write prompt_bridge
  back in as next work. Do not treat a missing memory_system package as a gap.
